00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.810
Everyone!

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.070
Welcome back.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.730
Hey, Ronja. We've got quite the haul today!

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.450
Wow. That sure is a lot.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:27.040
The magistrate had a few guards, but we took care of them easily!

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:28.960
Right?

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:29.840
You bet!

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:34.300
Why do the guards get in everyone's way?

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.100
Well that's because... umm...

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.520
It's sorta like this...

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.220
Ronja.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.610
Where does the rain fall from?

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:58.030
I have no idea. It's always seemed so natural that I've never even thought about it.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.540
Then, why do harpies attack people?

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:06.040
It's the same as rain. That's just the way they are.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:08.460
And we're the same.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:12.300
Whenever we do our job, Borka tries to steal it out from under us.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.050
Just like how we fight the Magistrate's guards.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:18.290
It's how we all fit into the big picture.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.390
I got it.

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.560
I see. You understand now.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:24.390
Yup.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:27.310
That's right. It's just like the rain.

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.400
Fjosok says some good things.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:05:00.900
If Borka wasn't such a scoundrel, I'd almost feel sorry for him.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:03.480
Why?

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:14.110
He doesn't get any peace these days, with the soldiers hunting him in Borka's Wood.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:19.700
They'll smoke him out of his robber's den soon enough.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.700
I've never seen a Borka robber before.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.160
That's a good thing, you know.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:32.250
The Borka robbers are all dirty devils, the lot of them.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:35.430
It's true that Borka is a scoundrel.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:39.510
So I couldn't care less if he gets beaten to a pulp by the soldiers.

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:45.760
But still...

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:51.070
What?

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:55.610
Borka's gang is full of scoundrels.

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:57.980
Yeah!

00:05:57.980 --> 00:05:59.070
That's right!

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:00.850
They're all scoundrels!

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:04.070
Good for nothing scoundrels!

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.830
I wonder how lucky I really am.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:13.120
To not be a Borka robber and a scoundrel.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.670
I'm quite lucky to be the daughter of the Mattis' robbers.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:26.390
Thank you, Ronja!

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:28.810
We'll do anything for you!

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:30.310
Uh-huh.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:32.770
Through fire, through water...

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.980
That brings back memories... That night when Ronja was born...

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:45.320
That sound sure was amazing.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:51.310
Our castle that was once one became two.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:55.040
It was split by a huge gap, right down the middle.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:00.340
That story again?

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:05.720
Oh my. What a pain the chief is when he's drunk.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.810
By the way, Ronja, do you remember what I told you?

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:20.050
To not fall into Hell's gap, right?

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:22.150
Yep, that's right!

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:28.830
It's split now, but we're still thankful for this castle.

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:32.490
We're as safe here as the fox in its lair and the eagle in its nest.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:35.780
No matter what kind of dumb soldiers come around,

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:39.040
we'll just shove 'em down to Hell with a mighty blow.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.220
Our castle is on top of the rockiest of mountains!

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:48.660
Yeah!

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:51.600
To the east, north, and west are steep cliffs!

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:52.040
Right!

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.850
There's no way anyone could scale it!

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:55.340
That's right!

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.730
Screw the guards!

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:02.650
If they come into Wolf's Neck...

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:19.460
Now!

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:41.040
Heave-ho!

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:45.940
Heave-ho!

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.630
Damn soldiers! Learned your lesson, huh?

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.080
If you did, then don't come back again!

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:00.940
If it means keeping you guys away, I'll do anything it takes!

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:03.340
Indeed!

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:06.420
I'll do anything it takes!

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:12.340
Ow!

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:16.060
Are you okay, Skalle-Per?

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.400
Oh, don't worry about me.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.480
But still, it's a hard thing to be old.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:28.920
Back in my day, I used to catch wolves by the dozen,

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:36.080
but now, the only thing I can
 catch are... fleas on my body.

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.840
It's about time to sleep, Ronja.

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:52.590
Good night.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:04.480
Let's head back...

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:06.770
to our rooms too.

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:09.650
Gramps, take it easy.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:15.370
Thanks for the help.

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:26.530
Pelje, take the leftovers to Knotas and Joen.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:27.940
Sure thing.

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:31.380
Klippen, you're in charge of water duty tomorrow.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:33.260
I know, I know.

